# AICL Example: Podcast Platform
# Audio processing, RSS feeds, transcription, ad insertion, analytics, and discovery

Goal
    Build a podcast platform that handles professional audio processing with loudness
    normalization and enhancement, manages RSS feed generation and distribution to all
    major directories, provides automated transcription with speaker diarization, supports
    dynamic ad insertion with targeting, delivers comprehensive analytics for creators,
    and powers content discovery through topic modeling and listener behavior analysis.

Constraint
    Audio processing must normalize to -16 LUFS for spoken content within 1 LU tolerance
    RSS feed generation must complete within 5 seconds of any episode metadata change
    Transcription must achieve at least 95% word accuracy for clear English speech
    Dynamic ad insertion must be seamless with no audible artifacts at splice points
    Analytics must be available within 5 minutes of listening event ingestion
    Discovery recommendations must be generated within 200ms per user request

Risk
    Audio normalization introduces artifacts or degrades speech intelligibility
Recovery
    Apply multi-pass normalization with speech-weighted filtering; validate output
    with PESQ score; if quality below threshold, fall back to simpler normalization;
    maintain original audio for reprocessing; alert audio engineering team on repeated failures

Risk
    RSS feed distribution delays cause episodes to be unavailable on directories
Recovery
    Implement webhook-based push notifications to directories; poll directories for
    feed update verification; if push fails, retry with exponential backoff; maintain
    direct submission API integration for major platforms; alert creator of distribution delay

Risk
    Transcription service outage blocks episode processing pipeline
Recovery
    Queue transcription jobs for deferred processing; mark episodes as transcription
    pending; enable episode publication without transcription; process transcription
    asynchronously when service recovers; notify creator when transcription available

Risk
    Ad insertion targeting leaks listener personal data to advertisers
Recovery
    Implement server-side ad decisioning with anonymized audience segments; never expose
    individual listener data; use differential privacy for audience reporting; audit ad
    targeting parameters for compliance; enforce data minimization in ad request payloads

Risk
    Analytics data inconsistency between real-time and batch-processed metrics
Recovery
    Use Lambda architecture with speed and batch layers; reconcile speed layer results
    with batch processing hourly; flag discrepancies exceeding 2% for investigation;
    serve speed layer data with appropriate confidence indicators; maintain immutable
    event log as source of truth

Risk
    Content discovery algorithm amplifies popular podcasts at expense of niche content
Recovery
    Implement diversity injection in recommendation ranking; allocate minimum 25% of
    recommendation slots to discovery content; track and optimize for catalog coverage;
    provide niche category boosting; monitor recommendation entropy metrics

Layer
    SubLayer: AudioLayer
        Audio ingestion, normalization, enhancement, format conversion, chapter marking
    SubLayer: FeedLayer
        RSS generation, directory distribution, feed validation, metadata management
    SubLayer: TranscriptionLayer
        Speech-to-text, speaker diarization, timestamp alignment, language detection
    SubLayer: AdLayer
        Ad decisioning, dynamic insertion, targeting, frequency capping, compliance
    SubLayer: AnalyticsLayer
        Event ingestion, metric computation, creator dashboard, export, benchmarking
    SubLayer: DiscoveryLayer
        Topic modeling, similarity matching, listener profiling, recommendation ranking

Validation
    All published audio must meet -16 LUFS loudness target within 1 LU tolerance
    RSS feeds must validate against Apple Podcasts and Spotify specifications
    Transcription timestamps must align within 500ms of actual speech boundaries
    Ad insertion splice points must be inaudible with crossfade validation
    Analytics event processing must maintain exactly-once semantics
    Discovery recommendations must include at least 25% catalog-diverse content
    All creator-facing metrics must be reconcilable to raw event data

Entity Podcast
    podcastId: string
    creatorId: string
    title: string
    description: string
    rssUrl: string
    coverArtUrl: string
    category: string
    subcategories: list
    language: string
    episodeCount: integer
    subscriberCount: integer
    createdAt: datetime
    rating: float

Entity Episode
    episodeId: string
    podcastId: string
    title: string
    description: string
    audioUrl: string
    duration: float
    fileSize: integer
    loudness: float
    publishDate: datetime
    season: integer
    episodeNumber: integer
    chapterMarks: list
    transcriptionId: string
    status: string

Entity Transcription
    transcriptionId: string
    episodeId: string
    language: string
    segments: list
    speakers: list
    wordAccuracy: float
    processingTime: float
    status: string
    createdAt: datetime
    reviewedBy: string

Entity AdCampaign
    campaignId: string
    advertiserId: string
    creativeUrl: string
    targetSegments: list
    frequencyCap: integer
    startDate: datetime
    endDate: datetime
    budget: float
    spent: float
    impressions: integer
    status: string

Entity ListeningEvent
    eventId: string
    listenerId: string
    episodeId: string
    podcastId: string
    eventType: string
    position: float
    duration: float
    timestamp: datetime
    deviceType: string
    client: string
    isAdSupported: boolean

Entity DiscoveryProfile
    listenerId: string
    listenedTopics: dict
    listenedCategories: dict
    completionRateAvg: float
    listeningVelocity: float
    noveltyAffinity: float
    recentPodcastIds: list
    embedding: list
    lastUpdated: datetime

Entity RSSFeed
    feedId: string
    podcastId: string
    feedUrl: string
    lastGenerated: datetime
    lastValidated: datetime
    validationErrors: list
    distributionStatus: dict
    subscriberCount: integer
    etag: string

Behavior ProcessAudio
    Input:
        episodeId: string
        sourceAudioPath: string
        processingOptions: dict
    Output:
        processedAudioUrl: string
        loudnessReport: dict
        chapterData: list
    Action:
        Ingest source audio and validate format compatibility
        Analyze audio: measure loudness, detect silence gaps, identify speech segments
        Apply loudness normalization to -16 LUFS with speech-weighted filtering
        Apply dynamic range compression optimized for spoken content
        Detect and mark chapter boundaries from silence gaps or metadata
        Convert to distribution formats (MP3, AAC, OGG) with appropriate bitrates
        Generate waveform data for visual player display
        Validate output quality with PESQ measurement
        Store processed audio in CDN with cache headers
        Return processed audio URLs with loudness and chapter reports

Behavior GenerateRSSFeed
    Input:
        podcastId: string
        includeDrafts: boolean
    Output:
        feedUrl: string
        feedHash: string
        validationResults: dict
    Action:
        Retrieve podcast metadata and all published episodes
        Build RSS 2.0 XML with Apple Podcasts and Spotify namespace extensions
        Include episode enclosures with correct MIME types and file sizes
        Add iTunes-specific tags (category, explicit, author, owner)
        Generate chapters and transcript references in feed entries
        Validate feed against Apple Podcasts and Spotify specifications
        Compute ETag for caching support
        Upload feed to CDN with appropriate cache TTL
        Push update notification to directory webhooks
        Return feed URL with validation results

Behavior TranscribeEpisode
    Input:
        episodeId: string
        audioUrl: string
        language: string
    Output:
        transcriptionId: string
        segments: list
        speakers: list
        accuracy: float
    Action:
        Retrieve audio and validate accessibility
        Detect language if not specified
        Perform speech-to-text with word-level timestamps
        Apply speaker diarization to identify distinct speakers
        Align timestamps with audio segments
        Calculate word-level confidence scores
        Compute overall accuracy estimate
        Flag low-confidence segments for human review
        Store transcription with episode reference
        Return transcription ID with segments and speaker data

Behavior InsertDynamicAd
    Input:
        episodeId: string
        listenerId: string
        insertionPoint: string
        context: dict
    Output:
        adCreativeUrl: string
        adDuration: float
        spliceMetadata: dict
    Action:
        Determine available ad slots at insertion point
        Query ad decisioning engine with anonymized listener segment
        Apply frequency capping per listener per campaign
        Select highest-value eligible ad campaign
        Generate splice metadata with crossfade parameters for seamless insertion
        Validate splice points are in silence or low-energy audio segments
        Record ad impression event for billing and analytics
        Return ad creative URL with splice instructions for client

Behavior ComputeAnalytics
    Input:
        podcastId: string
        periodStart: datetime
        periodEnd: datetime
        granularity: string
    Output:
        metrics: dict
        comparisons: dict
        benchmarks: dict
    Action:
        Aggregate listening events for podcast within time period
        Compute key metrics: total listens, unique listeners, completion rate, drop-off points
        Calculate subscriber growth and churn rates
        Identify top episodes by performance metrics
        Compute listening geography and device distributions
        Generate time-of-day and day-of-week listening patterns
        Compare against previous period for trend analysis
        Benchmark against category averages if available
        Prepare exportable report data
        Return comprehensive analytics with comparisons and benchmarks

Behavior GenerateDiscovery
    Input:
        listenerId: string
        context: dict
        maxResults: integer
    Output:
        podcastRecommendations: list
        episodeRecommendations: list
        categorySuggestions: list
    Action:
        Retrieve listener discovery profile and recent listening signals
        Generate candidate pool from collaborative and content-based sources
        Score candidates using topic similarity and listening pattern matching
        Inject diversity: ensure 25% of results are catalog-diverse discoveries
        Apply novelty weighting based on listener's exploration affinity
        Filter for language compatibility and content availability
        Rank by expected engagement with discovery bonus factor
        Cache results with activity-based TTL
        Return recommendations with explanation metadata

Behavior ValidateRSSCompliance
    Input:
        feedUrl: string
        targetPlatform: string
    Output:
        isValid: boolean
        errors: list
        warnings: list
        platformSpecificIssues: list
    Action:
        Fetch and parse RSS feed from URL
        Validate XML well-formedness and RSS 2.0 compliance
        Check required fields per target platform specification
        Validate enclosure URLs are accessible and correct MIME type
        Check cover art dimensions and file size requirements
        Verify iTunes namespace tags are correctly formatted
        Test feed accessibility and response time
        Generate compliance report with platform-specific requirements
        Return validation results with actionable error and warning lists

Condition
    When audio loudness deviates more than 1 LU from -16 LUFS target
    Then reprocess audio with adjusted normalization parameters; if still out
         of spec after second pass, flag for manual audio engineering review;
         do not publish episode until loudness is within tolerance

Condition
    When RSS feed validation fails for any major directory
    Then block episode publication, notify creator with specific validation errors,
         suggest corrections, and provide preview of feed output for manual review

Condition
    When listener ad frequency cap is reached for a campaign
    Then serve alternative ad from different campaign; if no eligible campaigns,
         serve house ad or skip ad slot entirely; never exceed frequency cap

Condition
    When transcription accuracy falls below 90% for an episode
    Then flag for human transcription review, display partial transcription with
         accuracy warning, and schedule re-transcription with enhanced model parameters

Condition
    When podcast analytics show listener drop-off exceeding 40% in first 5 minutes
    Then notify creator with drop-off analysis, suggest intro optimization,
         provide benchmark comparison, and highlight episodes with better retention

Event
    On EpisodePublished
    Action: Trigger RSS feed regeneration, notify subscribers via push, submit to
            podcast directories, start transcription pipeline, update discovery index,
            initialize analytics tracking

Event
    On TranscriptionCompleted
    Action: Update episode metadata with transcription reference, regenerate RSS feed
            with transcript tag, index transcription for search, notify creator of
            availability, enable chapter navigation

Event
    On AdImpression
    Action: Record impression for billing, update frequency cap counter, trigger
            analytics event, check campaign budget, update ad decisioning model

Event
    On ListeningMilestone
    Action: Check for achievement triggers, update listener profile, compute
            engagement metrics, update recommendation signals, generate creator
            notification for significant milestones

Event
    On FeedValidationError
    Action: Alert creator with error details, block feed distribution, provide
            fix suggestions, create support ticket, track resolution time

Parallel
    Audio processing pipeline across multiple episodes
    RSS feed generation and directory distribution
    Transcription processing with speech-to-text and diarization
    Dynamic ad insertion decisioning for concurrent listeners
    Analytics event aggregation and metric computation
    Discovery recommendation generation across listener segments

Optimize
    Target: Audio processing throughput
    Priority: Published episodes processed first; normalization is synchronous;
              format conversion can be parallelized per output format; quality
              validation must complete before CDN distribution

Optimize
    Target: Discovery recommendation relevance
    Priority: Listening completion signals weighted over start signals; topic
              consistency balanced with novelty; category diversity enforced;
              recent listening weighted higher than historical preferences

Learn
    Target: Audio processing parameters per content type
    Goal: Achieve optimal loudness normalization without speech artifacts for all content styles
    Adapt
        Based: Audio quality metrics from processed episodes, creator feedback on
               audio quality, listener playback device distributions, and loudness
               compliance verification results

Learn
    Target: Dynamic ad insertion effectiveness
    Goal: Maximize ad completion rate while maintaining listener retention above 95%
    Adapt
        Based: Ad skip rates by insertion point and content type, listener
               retention before and after ad breaks, and frequency cap optimization
               for engagement versus revenue tradeoffs

Learn
    Target: Discovery recommendation accuracy
    Goal: Achieve >40% click-through rate and >60% completion rate for recommended podcasts
    Adapt
        Based: Recommendation engagement metrics, listening pattern changes after
               discovery, category exploration velocity, and listener satisfaction
               signals from explicit ratings and subscriptions

Security
    Encrypt: Audio content in transit and at rest, transcription data, listener
             personal data, ad targeting segments, analytics event payloads
    Protect: Audio content integrity, RSS feed tampering prevention, ad insertion
             fraud detection, analytics event authenticity, transcription data privacy

Security
    Encrypt: Creator payout information, advertiser billing data, listener
             behavioral profiles, ad decisioning model parameters
    Protect: Ad frequency cap enforcement, listener data anonymization for
             ad targeting, content access control, download authentication,
             analytics manipulation prevention

Native Python
{
import hashlib
import time
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple
from enum import Enum
from datetime import datetime, timedelta

class EpisodeStatus(Enum):
    UPLOADING = "uploading"
    PROCESSING = "processing"
    TRANSCRIBING = "transcribing"
    READY = "ready"
    PUBLISHED = "published"
    ARCHIVED = "archived"

@dataclass
class Podcast:
    podcast_id: str
    creator_id: str
    title: str
    description: str
    rss_url: str
    cover_art_url: str
    category: str
    language: str
    episodes: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    subscriber_count: int = 0

@dataclass
class Episode:
    episode_id: str
    podcast_id: str
    title: str
    description: str
    audio_url: str
    duration: float
    file_size: int
    loudness_lufs: float
    publish_date: datetime
    season: int = 1
    episode_number: int = 0
    chapter_marks: List[dict] = field(default_factory=list)
    transcription_id: Optional[str] = None
    status: EpisodeStatus = EpisodeStatus.UPLOADING

@dataclass
class TranscriptionSegment:
    start_time: float
    end_time: float
    speaker: str
    text: str
    confidence: float

@dataclass
class Transcription:
    transcription_id: str
    episode_id: str
    language: str
    segments: List[TranscriptionSegment]
    speakers: List[str]
    overall_accuracy: float
    created_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)

class AudioProcessor:
    TARGET_LUFS = -16.0
    LUFS_TOLERANCE = 1.0

    def normalize_loudness(self, input_lufs: float, content: bytes) -> Tuple[float, bytes]:
        adjustment = self.TARGET_LUFS - input_lufs
        if abs(input_lufs - self.TARGET_LUFS) <= self.LUFS_TOLERANCE:
            return input_lufs, content
        # Apply gain adjustment (simplified)
        new_lufs = input_lufs + adjustment
        return new_lufs, content

    def validate_loudness(self, measured_lufs: float) -> bool:
        return abs(measured_lufs - self.TARGET_LUFS) <= self.LUFS_TOLERANCE

    def detect_chapters(self, silence_gaps: List[Tuple[float, float]],
                        min_gap_duration: float = 2.0) -> List[dict]:
        chapters = []
        chapter_start = 0.0
        for i, (start, end) in enumerate(silence_gaps):
            if end - start >= min_gap_duration:
                chapters.append({
                    "title": f"Chapter {i + 1}",
                    "start_time": chapter_start,
                    "end_time": start,
                })
                chapter_start = end
        return chapters

class RSSFeedGenerator:
    def generate_feed(self, podcast: Podcast, episodes: List[Episode]) -> str:
        items = []
        for ep in episodes:
            if ep.status != EpisodeStatus.PUBLISHED:
                continue
            items.append(f"""
    <item>
        <title>{ep.title}</title>
        <description>{ep.description}</description>
        <enclosure url="{ep.audio_url}" length="{ep.file_size}" type="audio/mpeg"/>
        <pubDate>{ep.publish_date.strftime('%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%S GMT')}</pubDate>
        <itunes:duration>{int(ep.duration)}</itunes:duration>
        <itunes:season>{ep.season}</itunes:season>
        <itunes:episode>{ep.episode_number}</itunes:episode>
    </item>""")

        return f"""<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:itunes="http://www.itunes.com/dtds/podcast-1.0.dtd">
<channel>
    <title>{podcast.title}</title>
    <description>{podcast.description}</description>
    <itunes:category text="{podcast.category}"/>
    <itunes:owner>
        <itunes:email>creator@platform.com</itunes:email>
    </itunes:owner>
    <language>{podcast.language}</language>
    {''.join(items)}
</channel>
</rss>"""

class AdDecisioningEngine:
    def select_ad(self, listener_segment: str, frequency_caps: Dict[str, int],
                  eligible_campaigns: List[dict]) -> Optional[dict]:
        for campaign in sorted(eligible_campaigns, key=lambda c: c.get("bid", 0), reverse=True):
            campaign_id = campaign["campaign_id"]
            if frequency_caps.get(campaign_id, 0) < campaign.get("frequency_cap", 3):
                return campaign
        return None
}
